From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Duran <15650777+carlos-duran@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] BananaDS: the LAN page's Players row shows with Host on the
 Mode row, greyed till Host is on

Q made Auto host with Host's size (wifi.local_players) and took Auto's own
Players row away. The Players row now shows only while the Mode row is on
Host. While Host is only picked there, not turned on yet, the row is
greyed with the saved count and says "Turn Host on to change it" when
selected: left, right and A do nothing, and Start hosting uses that count.
Once Host is on, it is editable as before (greyed while others are in the
session or a local wireless game is on). Off, Auto and Join don't show it.
---
 bananads/docs/SETTINGS.md | 2 +-
 bananads/src/menu.c       | 9 +++++----
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bananads/docs/SETTINGS.md b/bananads/docs/SETTINGS.md
index af62484..2c4771f 100644
--- a/bananads/docs/SETTINGS.md
+++ b/bananads/docs/SETTINGS.md
@@ -110,7 +110,7 @@ key can also come from the environment as `BANANADS_<KEY>` (dots become undersco
 | `kms.menu` | `on` | the in-game menu (src/menu.c: SuperDrastic's, in BananaOS's colours): the menu button pauses the game and opens it on both panels. Resume, Save and Load (8 slots with pictures; a load can be undone), Quick settings (volume, brightness, the microphone's meter and a blow, Cheats, LAN multiplayer, the emulator's options), Restart game, Quit game; in a local wireless game (`wifi.local`, another handheld in it) the game keeps running behind the menu (`kms.menu_live`) and Save, Load, Restart game and Cheats are off, as are F + R / F + L. `kms.menu_test=<n>` opens it 3 s in, on the main page (1), Save (2), Load (3), Quick settings (4) or the quit question (5), for tests |
 | `kms.menu_live` | `on` | in a local wireless game the menu opens over the running game instead of pausing it (a paused handheld stops answering and the others drop it): the game gets no buttons and no touch, the top screen behind the menu keeps the frame from the moment it opened, the sound goes on; Resume, Quick settings and Quit game work, the rest is off. Once the local game has been over for 3 s the game pauses and the menu is the usual one. `off`: the menu pauses, as before |
 | `kms.menu_live_volume` | `50` | the game's sound while the menu is open over it, in % (100: unchanged) |
-| (LAN multiplayer) | | the menu's Quick settings > LAN multiplayer page (builds with `BANANADS_LAN`): Mode Off / Auto / Host / Join, Players (Host: 2-16, 4 by default, while nobody else is in its session; Auto hosts with the same), Hosts found (Join: the hosts melonDS's LAN discovery hears on UDP 7063, each with its name, players and address; A joins one, the menu stays usable while it connects, up to 5 s, and says when it fails), the session's players with their ping, and Disconnect (Host and Join: a host's session ends, Off; a joined player goes back to looking for hosts). Auto has neither Players nor Disconnect: Off ends or leaves its session at once, Auto again starts afresh. With no Wi-Fi network, Quick settings' row says "No Wi-Fi" in grey and doesn't open; an open page turns its rows off and says to connect in BananaOS's Settings > Network. Auto says what it is doing: waiting for the game, looking for a host of this game, hosting, in a host's session (a desktop melonDS host said as such), the game online (WFC), or stopped by a problem (and when it tries again). The mode changes without a restart while no local wireless game is on; during one only Disconnect works (Auto: Off), after a question. The choice is kept in `wifi.local` and `wifi.local_players`; `BANANADS_WIFI_LOCAL` or `BANANADS_WIFI_LOCAL_PLAYERS` in the environment (BananaLinux: `/data/banana/bananads.env`) still win at each start, and the page says so while one is set |
+| (LAN multiplayer) | | the menu's Quick settings > LAN multiplayer page (builds with `BANANADS_LAN`): Mode Off / Auto / Host / Join, Players (only with Host on the Mode row: 2-16, 4 by default, changed once Host is on, while nobody else is in its session; greyed, "Turn Host on to change it", while Host is only picked; Auto hosts with the same), Hosts found (Join: the hosts melonDS's LAN discovery hears on UDP 7063, each with its name, players and address; A joins one, the menu stays usable while it connects, up to 5 s, and says when it fails), the session's players with their ping, and Disconnect (Host and Join: a host's session ends, Off; a joined player goes back to looking for hosts). Auto has neither Players nor Disconnect: Off ends or leaves its session at once, Auto again starts afresh. With no Wi-Fi network, Quick settings' row says "No Wi-Fi" in grey and doesn't open; an open page turns its rows off and says to connect in BananaOS's Settings > Network. Auto says what it is doing: waiting for the game, looking for a host of this game, hosting, in a host's session (a desktop melonDS host said as such), the game online (WFC), or stopped by a problem (and when it tries again). The mode changes without a restart while no local wireless game is on; during one only Disconnect works (Auto: Off), after a question. The choice is kept in `wifi.local` and `wifi.local_players`; `BANANADS_WIFI_LOCAL` or `BANANADS_WIFI_LOCAL_PLAYERS` in the environment (BananaLinux: `/data/banana/bananads.env`) still win at each start, and the page says so while one is set |
 | `kms.queue` | `2` | the most finished frames waiting for the screen (1-3); past that the oldest is dropped. Frames are committed one per refresh, so a game whose frames take 19 and 12 ms in turn still shows a new one at every refresh |
 | `kms.rt` | `on` | the presenter (the thread that commits the frames) at `SCHED_FIFO` 5, below the sound thread, as SuperDrastic's: a late wake-up finds the last flip still pending and the frame waits a refresh |
 | `kms.stats` | `0` | every this many frames shown, log the rate of new frames on the panels, the frames emulated per second, the refreshes that showed no new frame and the frames dropped |
diff --git a/bananads/src/menu.c b/bananads/src/menu.c
index abbf506..c59b638 100644
--- a/bananads/src/menu.c
+++ b/bananads/src/menu.c
@@ -785,7 +785,7 @@ static int lan_poll(void) {   /* the frontend's state into LS; 1: it changed */
 }
 static void lan_rows(void) {
     nlrows = 0; lrows[nlrows++] = LR_MODE;
-    if (lan_pick == BM_LAN_HOST || LS.mode == BM_LAN_HOST) lrows[nlrows++] = LR_PLAYERS;
+    if (lan_pick == BM_LAN_HOST) lrows[nlrows++] = LR_PLAYERS;   /* (the Mode row on Host; greyed till Host is on) */
     if (LS.mode == BM_LAN_JOIN && LS.state != BM_LAN_READY) lrows[nlrows++] = LR_HOSTS;
     if ((LS.mode == BM_LAN_HOST || LS.mode == BM_LAN_JOIN) && LS.state == BM_LAN_READY) lrows[nlrows++] = LR_LEAVE;
     if (sel_lan >= nlrows) sel_lan = nlrows - 1;
@@ -794,8 +794,8 @@ static void lan_open(void) {   /* Quick settings > LAN multiplayer */
     lan_poll(); lan_pick = LS.mode; lan_max_pick = LS.host_players >= 2 ? LS.host_players : 4; sel_lan = 0; lan_joining = 0;
     lan_rows();
 }
-/* the Players row (Host): the session's size, set before hosting (or again while alone in it); Auto uses it too */
-static int lan_players_off(void) { return lan_locked() || LS.no_net || (LS.mode == BM_LAN_HOST && LS.nplayers > 1); }
+/* the Players row (Host): the session's size, set once Host is on, while alone in it; Auto uses it too */
+static int lan_players_off(void) { return LS.mode != BM_LAN_HOST || lan_locked() || LS.no_net || LS.nplayers > 1; }
 static const char *lan_short(char *v, size_t n) {   /* Quick settings' value for the row */
     if (LS.no_net) snprintf(v, n, "No Wi-Fi");
     else if (LS.mode == BM_LAN_OFF) snprintf(v, n, "Off");
@@ -1014,7 +1014,7 @@ static void draw_bottom(void) {
                 if ((locked || LS.no_net) && !lan_auto_off_only()) snprintf(v, sizeof v, "%s", lan_mode_name[LS.mode]);
                 else { snprintf(v, sizeof v, "< %s >", lang_tr(lan_mode_name[lan_pick])); lang_keep(v); }
             } else if (id == LR_PLAYERS) {
-                if (lan_players_off()) snprintf(v, sizeof v, "%d", LS.max_players);
+                if (lan_players_off()) snprintf(v, sizeof v, "%d", LS.mode == BM_LAN_HOST ? LS.max_players : LS.host_players);
                 else snprintf(v, sizeof v, "< %d >", lan_max_pick);
             } else if (id == LR_HOSTS) {
                 if (LS.state == BM_LAN_BUSY && LS.addr[0]) snprintf(v, sizeof v, "Connecting...");
@@ -1210,6 +1210,7 @@ static void draw_bottom(void) {
     else if (s == SC_CHEAT) al = H.cheat_count(H.ctx) ? (H.cheat_get(H.ctx, sel_cheat) ? "Turn off" : "Turn on") : "Back";
     else if (s == SC_MIC) al = "Blow for 3 s";
     if (s == SC_MAIN) mid = "D-pad or tap";
+    if (s == SC_LAN && nlrows && lrows[sel_lan] == LR_PLAYERS && LS.mode != BM_LAN_HOST) mid = "Turn Host on to change it";
     /* the translator, where the menu's language shows (the file's translated-by: "简体中文 · Majirefy") */
     char credit[160];
     if (s == SC_SET && lang_active() && *lang_by()) {
